On Dec 4, 9:02 pm, Cuboidz <Dieter.Be...@gmail.com> wrote:
> I'm pretty new to Nethack, and I've come to dislike shops because of
> all the drudgery involved in putting them to good use: price-ID'ing
> scrolls, stealing stuff with your pet ...
>
> So I'm wondering whether it is feasible to just use shops for shopping
> only? And in the same vein: what do you (usually) do when you
> encounter a shop?

The only thing I price ID are identify scrolls.  I will sometimes try
on magic cloaks and/or magic boots.  I sometimes (very rarely) sell
random weapons/armor to the general store in Minetown, and I sometimes
(very rarely) sell gems to the general store in Minetown.

I don't actively try to steal from shops, because it's too much
effort.  The shopkeepers usually stay alive, unless I'm chaotic and
need to #offer them.  I don't think the protection racket is worth
doing unless I'm a Gnomish Healer, so I don't need shopkeeper money.
The Healers might sell random weapons/armor for protection money, but
they aren't going to steal because they want to get the protection
racket over with as soon as possible, and stealing takes too long.


